      "text": "{\"cards\":[{\"thesis\":\"Delaying Social Security can beat claiming early and investing the checks for retirees near average health, because guaranteed inflation adjusted payments are hard to replicate.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Claim early, invest the money, and markets will make waiting look foolish.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"Capturing the workplace retirement match before sending extra cash to moderate interest debt often wins, even after tax and investment risk are modeled.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Pay every debt down before investing for retirement at all.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"A low cost target date fund left comparable savers with competitive after tax wealth in history, not a forecast, versus chasing recent winners.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Managing your own funds should beat the boring default retirement option.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"Adding bonds during the final working stretch raised safe retirement income in bad historical sequences, history, not a forecast, even when average returns fell.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Stocks always make the best retirement portfolio if your horizon feels long.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"Strategic conversions from pretax retirement accounts during low income retirement years can reduce lifetime taxes, even for households already in modest brackets.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Conversions only help rich retirees facing very high future tax rates.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"Maxing tax advantaged retirement accounts before using taxable brokerage usually improves long horizon outcomes, despite withdrawal rules and reduced flexibility.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Taxable investing is almost as good because retirement accounts trap your money.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"For long horizon savers, investing extra cash often beat prepaying low rate mortgages in history, not a forecast, even after taxes and volatility.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"The mortgage is guaranteed debt, so prepaying must beat retirement investing.\\\"\"}]}"
